  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner who became paralyzed after a 2007 riding accident, died on 22 August following an accident in Jordan. Known for completing the 2012 London Marathon in a bionic suit over 17 days, she raised nearly £1m for charity. Lomas also lit the Paralympic cauldron in 2012 and completed the Great North Run in 2016 while pregnant, again using her bionic suit. Her family has requested privacy to grieve."
